  "interpretation": "Mean regional replacement is positive in 774 geographically and temporally matched species. Among the 72 species with support for both categorical contrasts, chromatic-chromatic replacement has a positive conditional interval; white-chromatic replacement and the direct paired difference both have intervals overlapping zero. This does NOT establish stronger chromatic geography or reject white-axis adaptation. The result is a cross-species photographic association, not a test of frequency-dependent fitness."
